30-second explanation

If your professor suddenly asks:

“What is your project?”

Say:

“My project is a Self-Healing GenAI Infrastructure for distributed microservices. The system monitors microservices using Prometheus and detects abnormal failures automatically. When an incident occurs, the Incident Manager collects operational evidence and sends it to a local GenAI model for root-cause diagnosis. The AI recommends a recovery, but it cannot directly execute infrastructure actions. A deterministic safety policy decides whether a predefined recovery action is safe. If approved, the system executes the action and verifies that the service has recovered. The entire incident and recovery process is stored in PostgreSQL and displayed on a monitoring dashboard.”

Then finish with:

“The key principle is: the LLM diagnoses, deterministic policy decides, and verification proves recovery.”

If your professor asks: "Why did you build this?"

Say:

“In distributed systems, failure in one service can affect other services. Traditional monitoring can detect the failure, but investigation and recovery often require human intervention. I wanted to explore whether GenAI could assist with incident diagnosis and whether predefined safety policies could allow controlled automated recovery.”

